# UAH Research Dashboard

Reconciled: 2026-10-08. Scope: research metadata and source navigation.
[HTML view](uah_research_dashboard.html), [registry](experiment_registry.json),
[artifact catalog](../artifacts/research/README.md).

## Authority and recorded boundaries

The [canonical masterplan](../plans/universal_agentic_harness_masterplan.md)
owns release order and gates. [NeuralWorkbench architecture](../architecture/neural_workbench_adaptive_ab_harness.md)
owns the adaptive research boundary. Dated investigations and reviews support
specific claims about their inspected bytes. This index is neither a second
roadmap nor an Observatory O1 runtime view.

The September Jev note proposes closed-candidate ranking. No executed UAH
Jev experiment is recorded here. H1 context persistence is an implementation
dependency named by the masterplan, distinct from H3 candidate context/retrieval
and H4 quarantined crystallization research. This catalog defines no context
tree, evidence-freshness rule or AB mapping.

The R0 receipt records executed diagnostics. The R1 review receipts concern a
compiler-only domain-pack identity repair, not all H0/H1 consumers or H2 parity.
Their observed values, original finding IDs and reviewed-byte identities remain
in the linked receipts. Live provider transport, model quality, owner-proven
effects and release qualification are separate evidence claims.

## Catalog

Record kinds describe document content, not a promotion ladder. A proposal
does not become an executed probe merely because it contains a test design.
An executed probe may be unsuccessful; a reviewed outcome may reject a change.
H-series dependencies are links, not declarations that prerequisites passed.
Scoring is `not_scored` in this metadata view; consult source receipts for their
actual observations. No direct comparability is inferred from labels or AB depth.

