## Using the sources

Consult the source before interpreting a catalog label. A source snapshot hash
identifies the indexed document bytes; it does not revalidate runtime provenance
or retrospectively approve other changes. Reference links are navigation only.
Update metadata only after the source document is complete, retain historical
evidence and regenerate both files. [Catalog rules](README.md) describe the
bounded update procedure.
